```sql
BEGIN;
UPDATE products SET stock = stock - 1
WHERE product_id = 1 AND stock >= 1;
-- 0 rows -> ROLLBACK, sold out
INSERT INTO orders (customer_id, product_id, qty, status)
VALUES (7, 1, 1, 'reserved');
COMMIT;
```
At read committed this is safe because the second UPDATE waits for the row lock, then re-evaluates the WHERE clause against the committed row.
